# Defect 507's class and panel 199's R3, ratified 2026-10-09: a correct
# program whose recursion ends on the `exit` of the function it is handed.
# Panel 199's R1 spares it, a call through a function value being one that
# may end the program (reading R4), and it prints 0, 1 and 2 and exits 0 at
# every level, with no clang warning since R3 (`-Wno-infinite-recursion`,
# the checker its witness). Reading R1 refused it (`callback` in the
# sitting).
function stop_at_three(n: i64)
    if n > 2
        exit(code: 0)
    print(n)

function turn(n: i64, act: (function(i64) -> ()))
    act(n)
    turn(n: n + 1, act: act)

function main()
    turn(n: 0, act: stop_at_three)
